GLOSSARY=[("AgentOps","Operating AI agents in production: tracing, SLOs, queues, budgets, incidents and releases."),
("AI-SPM","AI security posture management: inventory and misconfiguration scanning for models, endpoints, notebooks and AI data."),
("Cedar","An authorization policy language (principal, action, resource, conditions) with formal analysis; used by Amazon Verified Permissions."),
("CDC","Change data capture: streaming inserts, updates and deletes from a database's transaction log."),
("Circuit breaker (data)","A check that stops agents from answering or acting on data that failed freshness or quality checks."),
("CSPM","Cloud security posture management: continuous scanning of cloud configurations against policies and benchmarks."),
("Data contract","A versioned, enforced agreement on a dataset's schema, semantics, quality and freshness."),
("Data product","A dataset with an owner, contract, SLOs, documentation and interfaces, published for reuse."),
("Digital Omnibus on AI","Regulation (EU) 2026/1744, which amended the EU AI Act and moved high-risk obligations to Dec 2027 (Annex III) and Aug 2028 (Annex I)."),
("Durable execution","Workflow engines that persist each step so long-running agents resume after crashes."),
("Forward Deployed Engineer","An engineer embedded with customers who builds and ships production systems in their environment."),
("Golden set","A curated, versioned eval dataset with expected outputs or rubrics."),
("Kill switch","A control that instantly disables a tool, agent, tenant or autonomy level, enforced outside the model."),
("Lakehouse","Object storage plus open table formats (Iceberg, Delta) giving warehouse-like tables on open files."),
("Lethal trifecta","An agent with private data access, exposure to untrusted content and an exfiltration channel."),
("Lineage","A record of how datasets are derived from sources and where they flow, ideally column-level."),
("Medallion architecture","Bronze (raw), silver (cleaned) and gold (business-ready) data layers."),
("NIST AI RMF","NIST's voluntary AI risk framework with functions Govern, Map, Measure and Manage."),
("OPA / Rego","Open Policy Agent and its declarative policy language, used for CI, admission and API authorization."),
("OpenLineage","An open standard for lineage events emitted by data jobs."),
("pass^k","The probability an agent succeeds on all k independent attempts; measures reliability."),
("Policy as code","Rules expressed in a policy language, versioned, tested and enforced by an engine."),
("ReBAC","Relationship-based access control (Zanzibar-style), e.g. OpenFGA or SpiceDB."),
("Semantic layer","A layer that defines metrics and dimensions once and compiles requests into correct SQL."),
("Workload identity","Short-lived cloud credentials bound to a workload (pod/service) instead of static keys."),
("WORM storage","Write-once-read-many storage (e.g. object lock) for tamper-evident records.")]
